WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:01.839
Good morning Hank it's Tuesday!

00:00:01.839 --> 00:00:07.279
So many Nerdfighters made amazing book towers
that I figured I should give it a try myself

00:00:07.279 --> 00:00:08.809
so let's head up to the library.

00:00:08.809 --> 00:00:10.170
By the way Hank, I have a library.

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:14.079
While I have this voice-over opportunity,
I want to recommend three recent reads.

00:00:14.079 --> 00:00:18.450
First Ta-Nehisi Coates's amazing book Between
the World and Me which I cannot stop thinking

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:19.450
about.

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:22.179
Second, The Bail Trap link in the dooblydoo
an article in The New York Times that explores

00:00:22.179 --> 00:00:26.470
one of the reasons people in poverty are disproportionately
imprisoned in the United States.

00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:30.300
And third, another article in The New York
Times about a fourteen year old boy locked

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:34.340
in solitary confinement which I found chilling
and deeply upsetting.

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:38.160
Also since those are all tough reads, I recommend
a GIF of a puppy jumping for the first time,

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:39.230
link in the dooblydoo.

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:40.810
AAAHHH Dangit!!

00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:46.480
Well there you have it Hank, couldn't build
a house of cards in 2007 and can't build a

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:49.860
house of books in 2015, some things never
change.

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:53.870
Okay, insert artful transition here, Hank
I took the Nerdfighter Census survey yesterday,

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:57.470
great survey as always but I felt like some
of the questions weren't inclusive of me,

00:00:57.470 --> 00:00:59.800
like the question "Do you follow John on Twitter?"

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:03.330
I just didn't know how to answer that because
technically I don't, but I also kinda feel

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:04.330
like I do.

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:05.910
I mean, I see most of John's tweets.

00:01:05.910 --> 00:01:09.320
Also, you asked me whether I watch videos
at school, which I don't, because that would

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:12.460
be creepy, but not whether I watch videos
at work.

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:17.110
Which I do because technically, like, watching
Akilah Hughes get drunk and review books is

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:19.970
my job, well that and semi-professional FIFA
playing.

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:25.670
Speaking of which Hank, behold the wonder
of the John Green Stand at AFC Wimbledon's

00:01:25.670 --> 00:01:26.670
stadium.

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:29.890
Okay Hank but there was one question I did
not appreciate at all, question twenty five,

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:34.530
the one where you pit my beautiful unwavering
puff against your fancy new hair style by

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:37.530
asking "Who has better hair, Hank or John?".

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:41.050
Now Hank we use the Nerdfighter Census every
year to figure out what topics we should cover

00:01:41.050 --> 00:01:44.780
on Crash Course and what sort of videos we
should make on Vlogbrothers and it helps us

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:47.260
to understand the interests and passions of
Nerdfighteria

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:51.549
and I'm so grateful to everyone who fills
it out but I don't want to submit my hair

00:01:51.549 --> 00:01:53.230
to a popular vote.

00:01:53.230 --> 00:01:57.311
In fact Hank, just seeing that question made
me go out and and get this haircut, and I'm

00:01:57.311 --> 00:02:01.260
worried that soon, in an attempt to impress
Nerdfighteria and win their pileous support,

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:05.630
we'll have an ever escalating arms race, like
the US and the Soviets did in the 1980s, only

00:02:05.630 --> 00:02:07.560
with hair instead of nuclear weapons.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:10.619
Until eventually one of us goes bankrupt and
our empire collapses.

00:02:10.619 --> 00:02:11.870
Is that what you want Hank?

00:02:11.870 --> 00:02:15.209
And yes, I did just use the word pileous,
meaning of or relating to hair.

00:02:15.209 --> 00:02:18.359
This whole hair thing is making me so anxious
that my vocabulary is coming out.

00:02:18.359 --> 00:02:22.060
Hank, one of the weirdest and most beautiful
things about Nerdfighteria is that in eight

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:25.620
years, they've never allowed us to have, like,
a proper sibling rivalry.

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:30.529
It's never been about Team Hank or Team John,
it's always been about Team Hank And John.

00:02:30.529 --> 00:02:32.819
Or as I prefer to think of it, Team John And
Hank.

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:36.400
But you put that question in the survey Hank,
so I guess you want a contest, and you're

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:37.459
gonna get one.

00:02:37.459 --> 00:02:39.159
Here's the thing about John's hair, Hank.

00:02:39.159 --> 00:02:43.140
You may not always agree with it, but you
have to respect it's honesty.

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:48.060
John's hair, the Puff, has remained fundamentally
unchanged over the last eight years, it grows

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:52.689
and shrinks with my anxiety levels but at
it's core, the Puff is the Puff.

00:02:52.689 --> 00:02:57.409
This is hair without product or artifice or
gimmicks, I'm not sure you can say that about

00:02:57.409 --> 00:02:59.889
Hank's hair, but I'm not going to run a negative
campaign.

00:02:59.889 --> 00:03:03.040
You're never going to hear me say "Hank, what's
it like having a haircut that Tyler Oakley

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:04.780
discarded in 2011?"

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:08.099
And I would never point out that Hank has
the haircut of a young Republican and the

00:03:08.099 --> 00:03:10.329
face of a de-mustachioed Leon Trotsky.

00:03:10.329 --> 00:03:14.400
Nope, you'll never hear that from me because
my hair is keeping it positive.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:19.230
Let me just submit that a vote for John's
hair is a vote for stability, and brotherhood,

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:20.230
and unity.

00:03:20.230 --> 00:03:24.980
So friends, please fill out the 2015 Nerdfighter
Census, and when you do, consider the Puff.

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:28.450
Also if you have a job please fill out the
Nerdfighter Census because right now I can't

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:35.040
tell if it's selection bias or if the unemployment
rate in Nerdfighteria is actually 85 percent,

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:38.900
which would be quite worrisome, it would put
us at the very bottom of like, uh, all countries.

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:41.849
Hank, you're a good brother and you have good
hair.

00:03:41.849 --> 00:03:43.739
It's just not this good.

00:03:43.739 --> 00:03:44.489
I'll see you on Friday.

